502
00:19:42,415 --> 00:19:43,417
CROW:
Dress for less?

503
00:19:43,450 --> 00:19:45,052
Did I...?

504
00:19:45,085 --> 00:19:49,857
- If thou didst ever
thy dear father love...

505
00:19:49,890 --> 00:19:52,125
- Oh, heaven!

506
00:19:52,192 --> 00:19:55,562
- ...revenge his murder.

507
00:19:55,595 --> 00:19:56,563
- Murder!

508
00:19:57,663 --> 00:19:59,232
- Murder most foul.

509
00:19:59,265 --> 00:20:02,202
CROW: He killed a chicken?
- Haste me to know it

510
00:20:02,235 --> 00:20:04,203
that I, with wings
as swift as meditation

511
00:20:04,237 --> 00:20:05,405
or the thoughts of love,

512
00:20:05,438 --> 00:20:07,840
may sweep to my revenge.

513
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:10,577
- 'Tis given out that,
sleeping in my orchard,

514
00:20:10,610 --> 00:20:12,045
a serpent stung me...

515
00:20:12,078 --> 00:20:13,047
SERVO:
Cut to the ghost.

516
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:14,848
The ghost!
Cut to the ghost!

517
00:20:14,882 --> 00:20:19,285
- ...thy father's life
now wears his crown.

518
00:20:19,318 --> 00:20:20,553
- Oh, my prophetic soul!

519
00:20:20,587 --> 00:20:22,622
My uncle.

520
00:20:22,655 --> 00:20:27,060
- Aye, that incestuous beast
won to his shameful lust

521
00:20:27,093 --> 00:20:29,930
the will of my most
seeming-virtuous queen.

522
00:20:29,963 --> 00:20:31,798
CROW:
That's what I am.

523
00:20:31,832 --> 00:20:35,268
- Sleeping within my orchard
upon my secure hour,

524
00:20:35,302 --> 00:20:39,773
thy uncle stole
with juice of cursed hebenon

525
00:20:39,807 --> 00:20:44,110
in a vial and in the porches of
my ears...

526
00:20:44,143 --> 00:20:47,113
CROW: To the ghost!
- ...poured leprous distilment.

527
00:20:47,147 --> 00:20:49,750
MIKE:
Oh, hang on.
I'm passin' a stone. Ooh.

528
00:20:49,783 --> 00:20:53,453
- Thus was I, sleeping,
by a brother's hand of life...

529
00:21:06,065 --> 00:21:07,633
SERVO:
Oh, boy, this
"ghost of Mike's father"

530
00:21:07,667 --> 00:21:09,002
gag is too good!

531
00:21:09,035 --> 00:21:11,137
CROW:
Yep, no question,
a brilliantly conceived,

532
00:21:11,170 --> 00:21:13,773
perfectly executed
bit of tomfoolery.

533
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:15,475
- Hello?
SERVO: Aaah! A ghost! Help me!

534
00:21:15,475 --> 00:21:16,610
CROW:
Servo, it's just Mike.

535
00:21:16,677 --> 00:21:17,943
SERVO:
Oh, okay.

536
00:21:18,012 --> 00:21:18,978
[COUGHS]

537
00:21:19,012 --> 00:21:21,113
Mark me,
for I am your father's ghost

538
00:21:21,147 --> 00:21:22,682
come to tell you...
- Whoa, wait a minute.

539
00:21:22,715 --> 00:21:23,683
No. Can't be my father.

540
00:21:23,717 --> 00:21:24,918
He's alive and well.

541
00:21:24,952 --> 00:21:27,653
Owns a mail-order burlap store
out in Minong, Wisconsin.

542
00:21:27,687 --> 00:21:28,955
SERVO:
D'oh! We didn't check on that.

543
00:21:28,988 --> 00:21:31,090
Ugh. Okay, okay,
try his Uncle Les.

544
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:32,092
I'm pretty sure he's dead.

545
00:21:32,125 --> 00:21:33,693
CROW:
I'm your Uncle Les, come to...

546
00:21:33,727 --> 00:21:34,795
- Oh, no, no. Retired.

547
00:21:34,828 --> 00:21:35,995
Lives in McAllen, Texas.

548
00:21:36,028 --> 00:21:37,297
You know, Pearl just forwarded

549
00:21:37,330 --> 00:21:39,365
another of his delightful
Christmas letters.

550
00:21:39,398 --> 00:21:40,767
SERVO:
Cousin Al! Cousin Al!

551
00:21:40,800 --> 00:21:42,802
CROW:
Okay. I'm your cousin Al,
dead more these two months...

552
00:21:42,835 --> 00:21:44,537
- Oh, no, no.
He's alive.

553
00:21:44,570 --> 00:21:46,873
He rebuilds carburetors
out of a pole shed

554
00:21:46,907 --> 00:21:48,275
in Sauk Rapids, Minnesota.

555
00:21:48,308 --> 00:21:49,542
Just sent me a price list.

556
00:21:49,575 --> 00:21:50,743
You know, you can
get a pretty good deal...

557
00:21:50,777 --> 00:21:52,245
- Any leads there,
other part of the ghost?

558
00:21:52,278 --> 00:21:53,913
SERVO:
Uh, uh, uh...
okay, okay, okay.

559
00:21:53,947 --> 00:21:55,348
Brother-in-law's
ex-wife Wanda?

560
00:21:55,382 --> 00:21:57,217
CROW:
Okay. I am your
brother-in-laws...

561
00:21:57,250 --> 00:21:58,218
- Oh, no. Not Wanda.

562
00:21:58,252 --> 00:22:00,053
She works a pit crew
up to Brainerd.

563
00:22:00,087 --> 00:22:02,288
She can hurl a tire 35 feet
without even breathing hard.

564
00:22:02,322 --> 00:22:03,990
CROW: [SIGHS]
Don't your relatives ever die?

565
00:22:04,023 --> 00:22:06,025
It's over.
Hit it, Cousin Wanda.

566
00:22:06,058 --> 00:22:07,460
SERVO:
First try his brother Ron's

567
00:22:07,493 --> 00:22:08,662
karate teacher Herb Dowdy.

568
00:22:08,695 --> 00:22:10,763
CROW: Put a sock in it.
SERVO: No! Let me go. Watch it!

569
00:22:10,797 --> 00:22:11,765
CROW: You cut it out.
SERVO: Ow! Ow!

570
00:22:11,798 --> 00:22:13,367
- We'll be right back.

571
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:14,702
[ALL YELLING]

572
00:22:16,903 --> 00:22:19,907
[♪♪♪]

573
00:22:23,877 --> 00:22:25,278
MIKE:
It's supposed to be a duck.

574
00:22:28,648 --> 00:22:29,817
CROW:
I love life.

575
00:22:31,852 --> 00:22:33,018
Oh, yeah, that was hilarious.

576
00:22:33,053 --> 00:22:34,053
Any way.

577
00:22:37,623 --> 00:22:39,658
MIKE:
She stitched her hand
to her knee.

578
00:22:41,695 --> 00:22:44,898
CROW: [GROWLING]
Mmm, friend, huh.

579
00:22:47,367 --> 00:22:49,435
SERVO:
Oh, I stuck a fork
in the outlet.

580
00:22:51,405 --> 00:22:53,940
MIKE:
How 'bout some
spiral-cut Hamlet?

581
00:22:57,277 --> 00:22:58,878
CROW:
Get thee to a bakery.

582
00:22:58,912 --> 00:23:00,813
No wait...
- [GASPS]

583
00:23:02,315 --> 00:23:03,283
SERVO:
Ooh.

584
00:23:03,317 --> 00:23:05,385
He's doing a Danish mind meld.

585
00:23:08,822 --> 00:23:11,023
CROW:
Don't look.
It's your Christmas present.

586
00:23:13,493 --> 00:23:14,762
MIKE:
Oh, man! Me and Horatio

587
00:23:14,795 --> 00:23:16,497
got blasted on Aquavit,

588
00:23:16,530 --> 00:23:19,232
woke up on the express bus
to Copenhagen.

589
00:23:19,265 --> 00:23:20,467
Ugh.

590
00:23:23,970 --> 00:23:24,938
SERVO:
What is it, boy?

591
00:23:24,972 --> 00:23:26,072
Uncle killed dad?

592
00:23:26,105 --> 00:23:27,107
Hmm?

593
00:23:34,080 --> 00:23:36,617
MIKE:
Well, I'm gonna take off,
I guess.

594
00:23:37,850 --> 00:23:40,620
So, okay then.

595
00:23:42,755 --> 00:23:45,092
CROW:
Dad! Hamlet's looking at me.

596
00:23:49,328 --> 00:23:50,763
- How now, Ophelia!
What's the matter?

597
00:23:50,797 --> 00:23:52,165
- I have been so affrighted.

598
00:23:52,198 --> 00:23:53,600
- With what,
in the name of God?

599
00:23:53,633 --> 00:23:54,767
SERVO:
Your hair.

600
00:23:54,802 --> 00:23:57,137
- As I was sewing in my closet,
my lord, Hamlet...

601
00:23:57,137 --> 00:23:58,705
MIKE:
She was sewing in her closet?

602
00:23:58,738 --> 00:24:01,542
- ...with his doublet all
unbraced, pale as his shirt,

603
00:24:01,608 --> 00:24:03,243
his knees
knocking each other,

604
00:24:03,243 --> 00:24:05,978
and with a look
so piteous in purport,

605
00:24:06,012 --> 00:24:07,113
he comes before me.

606
00:24:07,147 --> 00:24:08,615
CROW:
No one likes a tattletale,
Ophelia.

607
00:24:08,648 --> 00:24:12,052
- Mad for thy love?

608
00:24:12,085 --> 00:24:17,890
- My lord, I do not know,
but truly I do fear it.

609
00:24:17,923 --> 00:24:19,725
SERVO:
I'm gonna get my hair re-lumped.

610
00:24:22,162 --> 00:24:24,263
CROW:
Honey, what happened
to all the ear poison?

611
00:24:27,867 --> 00:24:29,035
MIKE:
Boom!

612
00:24:29,068 --> 00:24:30,137
SERVO:
Yeah.

613
00:24:32,405 --> 00:24:33,940
CROW:
What is it,
Cold Water on the Groin...

614
00:24:33,973 --> 00:24:35,208
I mean, Polonius?

615
00:24:38,478 --> 00:24:41,047
- My lord, I do think
that I have found the very cause

616
00:24:41,080 --> 00:24:42,482
of Hamlet's lunacy.

617
00:24:42,515 --> 00:24:43,850
MIKE:
He's insane.

618
00:24:43,883 --> 00:24:45,485
- Oh, speak of that.

619
00:24:45,518 --> 00:24:47,753
That do I long to hear.

620
00:24:47,787 --> 00:24:49,455
Thou still has been
the father of good news.

621
00:24:49,488 --> 00:24:50,457
- Have I, my lord?

622
00:24:50,490 --> 00:24:51,658
I assure my good liege.

623
00:24:51,692 --> 00:24:53,260
I hold my duty
as I hold my soul

624
00:24:53,293 --> 00:24:55,462
both to my God
and to my gracious king.

625
00:24:55,495 --> 00:24:57,663
SERVO:
I know nothing.

626
00:24:57,697 --> 00:24:59,398
- He tells me, my dear Gertrude,
he hath found

627
00:24:59,432 --> 00:25:01,868
the source of
all your son's distemper.

628
00:25:01,902 --> 00:25:03,837
- I doubt it is no other
but the main:

629
00:25:03,870 --> 00:25:08,742
his father's death
and our o'er hasty marriage.

630
00:25:08,775 --> 00:25:09,742
MIKE: Hi!
- My liege and madam,

631
00:25:09,775 --> 00:25:12,178
your noble son is mad.

632
00:25:12,212 --> 00:25:15,448
Mad call I it for to define
true madness what is't

633
00:25:15,482 --> 00:25:16,950
but to be nothing else but mad.

634
00:25:16,983 --> 00:25:18,485
- More matter with less art.

635
00:25:18,518 --> 00:25:19,818
- Madam, I use no art at all.

636
00:25:19,852 --> 00:25:21,220
That he is mad 'tis true.

637
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:24,057
'Tis true, 'tis pity,
and pity 'tis 'tis true.

638
00:25:24,090 --> 00:25:25,625
Thus it remains...

639
00:25:26,727 --> 00:25:27,727
CROW:
They had huge balance beams
back then.

640
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:29,095
Look at that.

641
00:25:32,165 --> 00:25:34,867
MIKE:
Ah, she's logging names
into her Palm Pilot.

642
00:25:38,238 --> 00:25:40,240
SERVO:
Honey, check this out.

643
00:25:40,273 --> 00:25:41,775
'Ah, so. I Japanese.'

644
00:25:41,808 --> 00:25:43,175
Huh! Sorry.

645
00:25:45,512 --> 00:25:47,613
CROW:
Please pray for me
while I shower.

646
00:25:50,717 --> 00:25:53,185
SERVO:
What the Shroud of Turin sees.

647
00:25:58,090 --> 00:25:59,058
CROW:
The nuns sent me home.

648
00:25:59,092 --> 00:26:01,093
My skirt is too short.

649
00:26:03,797 --> 00:26:10,070
- Nymph, in thy orisons
be all my sins remembered.

650
00:26:11,537 --> 00:26:12,638
MIKE:
Whoo!

651
00:26:12,672 --> 00:26:14,907
The "orison" line
sucked the air out of the room.

652
00:26:14,942 --> 00:26:16,008
[WHISTLES]

653
00:26:16,042 --> 00:26:17,010
- My prince...

654
00:26:17,043 --> 00:26:18,678
SERVO:
...are back from Photo Mat.

655
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:24,117
- How does your honor
for this many a day?

656
00:26:24,150 --> 00:26:25,118
CROW:
I don't know.

657
00:26:25,152 --> 00:26:26,152
Okay, I guess.

658
00:26:26,185 --> 00:26:28,388
- I humbly thank you. Well.

659
00:26:28,422 --> 00:26:31,257
MIKE:
But could you please
return my pants?

660
00:26:31,290 --> 00:26:32,258
- My prince...

661
00:26:32,292 --> 00:26:33,760
SERVO:
...didn't come out that well.

662
00:26:36,295 --> 00:26:38,665
MIKE:
Ooh, the bench smells funny.

663
00:26:38,698 --> 00:26:41,033
- ...I have remembrances
of yours

664
00:26:41,067 --> 00:26:44,503
that I have longed long
to re-deliver.

665
00:26:44,537 --> 00:26:46,740
I pray you now receive them.

666
00:26:46,773 --> 00:26:49,108
- Not I.
I never gave you aught.

667
00:26:49,142 --> 00:26:50,443
CROW:
Tcha!

668
00:26:50,477 --> 00:26:54,280
- My honored prince, you know
right well you did...

669
00:26:54,313 --> 00:26:55,882
SERVO:
Right well did not.

670
00:26:55,915 --> 00:26:57,283
- ...in words
of so sweet breath composed

671
00:26:57,317 --> 00:27:01,855
as made the things more rich,
their perfume lost.

672
00:27:01,888 --> 00:27:05,092
Take these again,
for to the noble mind

673
00:27:05,125 --> 00:27:08,695
rich gifts wax poor
when givers prove unkind.

674
00:27:08,728 --> 00:27:09,928
There my lord.

675
00:27:09,962 --> 00:27:10,930
MIKE:
Okay, fine.

676
00:27:10,963 --> 00:27:11,965
I'll throw them away.

677
00:27:14,100 --> 00:27:16,268
- Are you honest?
CROW: Yes. No. I lied!

678
00:27:16,302 --> 00:27:17,937
- Are you honest?

679
00:27:17,970 --> 00:27:19,405
- My lord?

680
00:27:19,438 --> 00:27:21,540
- Are you fair?

681
00:27:21,573 --> 00:27:24,310
- What means your lordship?

682
00:27:24,343 --> 00:27:27,013
- That if you be
honest and fair,

683
00:27:27,047 --> 00:27:30,617
your honesty should admit
no discourse to your beauty.

684
00:27:30,650 --> 00:27:32,818
- Could beauty
have better commerce,

685
00:27:32,852 --> 00:27:34,853
my prince, than with honesty?

686
00:27:34,887 --> 00:27:35,955
- Aye, truly...

687
00:27:35,988 --> 00:27:37,257
CROW:
Yeah, you know, what you said.

688
00:27:37,290 --> 00:27:39,392
- ...for the power of beauty
will sooner transform honesty

689
00:27:39,425 --> 00:27:40,493
from what it is to a bawd

690
00:27:40,527 --> 00:27:42,228
than the force of honesty
can translate beauty

691
00:27:42,262 --> 00:27:43,530
into his likeness.

692
00:27:43,563 --> 00:27:45,632
This was sometime a paradox,

693
00:27:45,665 --> 00:27:48,635
but now the time
gives it proof.

694
00:27:48,668 --> 00:27:50,303
MIKE:
Huh? What do you think
of them apples?

695
00:27:52,438 --> 00:27:54,540
[SPITTING]

696
00:27:54,573 --> 00:27:57,410
- I did love you once.

697
00:27:57,443 --> 00:27:59,578
- Aye, my prince.

698
00:27:59,612 --> 00:28:01,447
You made me believe so.

699
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:03,048
- You should not have
believed me.

700
00:28:03,082 --> 00:28:04,450
I loved you not.

701
00:28:04,517 --> 00:28:06,685
MIKE:
Well, I always thought
you were gay.

702
00:28:06,753 --> 00:28:08,822
- I was the more deceived.

703
00:28:09,955 --> 00:28:11,792
- Get thee to a nunnery.

704
00:28:11,825 --> 00:28:13,727
Why wouldst thou be
a breeder of sinners?

705
00:28:13,760 --> 00:28:15,262
CROW:
Be a breeder of schnauzers.

706
00:28:15,295 --> 00:28:17,297
- I am myself indifferent
honest,

707
00:28:17,330 --> 00:28:18,832
but yet I could accuse me
of such things

708
00:28:18,865 --> 00:28:21,667
that it were better
my mother had not borne me.

709
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:24,803
I am very proud,
revengeful, ambitious.

710
00:28:24,837 --> 00:28:26,138
SERVO:
Ooh, he's Republican.

711
00:28:26,172 --> 00:28:29,175
- We are errant knaves, all.

712
00:28:29,208 --> 00:28:30,677
Believe none of us.

713
00:28:30,710 --> 00:28:32,545
MIKE:
Can you set me up with Horatio?

714
00:28:34,047 --> 00:28:36,582
CROW:
Heh! I shut her down, man.

715
00:28:40,587 --> 00:28:42,122
- [WHISPERING]
Where's your father?

716
00:28:42,155 --> 00:28:44,223
SERVO: [WHISPERING]
Bastard owes me ten kronors.

717
00:28:46,258 --> 00:28:47,793
- At home, my lord.

718
00:28:47,827 --> 00:28:50,997
CROW:
Ophelia, Sam Wainwright's
on the phone!

719
00:28:51,030 --> 00:28:52,765
- Let the doors
be shut upon him

720
00:28:52,798 --> 00:28:55,602
that he may play the fool
nowhere but in his own house!

721
00:28:55,635 --> 00:28:56,602
[SOBBING]

722
00:28:56,635 --> 00:28:58,170
MIKE:
Whoa. Jackson Browne-let.

723
00:28:58,203 --> 00:28:59,905
[SOBBING]

724
00:28:59,938 --> 00:29:01,207
CROW:
Thank you, but I don't need CPR.

725
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:02,242
Thank you.

726
00:29:04,043 --> 00:29:05,778
[GASPING]

727
00:29:05,812 --> 00:29:07,280
- If thou dost marry,

728
00:29:07,313 --> 00:29:09,582
I'll give thee
this plague for thy dowry:

729
00:29:09,615 --> 00:29:11,918
be thou as chaste as ice,
as pure as snow,

730
00:29:11,952 --> 00:29:13,887
thou shall not escape calumny.

731
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:14,887
Get thee to a nunnery.

732
00:29:14,920 --> 00:29:15,955
Go! Farewell!

733
00:29:15,988 --> 00:29:16,957
SERVO:
You're doing fine, honey!

734
00:29:16,990 --> 00:29:18,992
He's all yours.
You got him.

735
00:29:19,025 --> 00:29:19,992
[GASPING, SOBBING]

736
00:29:20,025 --> 00:29:22,328
- Or if thou wilt needs marry,
marry a fool

737
00:29:22,362 --> 00:29:26,332
for wise men know well enough
what monsters you make of them.

738
00:29:26,365 --> 00:29:27,733
To a nunnery go. Farewell!

739
00:29:27,800 --> 00:29:30,068
MIKE:
Gah!
Just gets my tights in a bundle.

740
00:29:30,137 --> 00:29:33,105
- Oh, heavenly powers
restore him!

741
00:29:33,138 --> 00:29:35,808
- I've heard of your paintings
too, well enough.

742
00:29:35,842 --> 00:29:37,543
God has given you one face

743
00:29:37,577 --> 00:29:39,645
and you make yourselves another.

744
00:29:39,678 --> 00:29:41,647
You jig, you amble,
and you lisp,

745
00:29:41,680 --> 00:29:43,650
you nickname God's creatures...

746
00:29:43,683 --> 00:29:45,685
and make your wantonness
your ignorance.

747
00:29:45,718 --> 00:29:47,120
Go to, I'll no more on't.

748
00:29:47,153 --> 00:29:48,453
It hath made me mad.

749
00:29:48,488 --> 00:29:49,788
That hath made me mad!

750
00:29:49,822 --> 00:29:51,057
CROW:
I'm not here!

751
00:29:51,090 --> 00:29:53,760
- I say we will have
no more marriages.

752
00:29:53,793 --> 00:29:55,195
Those that are married,

753
00:29:55,228 --> 00:30:00,833
all - all but one
- shall long live.

754
00:30:00,867 --> 00:30:03,235
The rest shall
keep as they are.

755
00:30:03,268 --> 00:30:04,637
CROW:
I am back. You miss me?

756
00:30:06,772 --> 00:30:08,775
- To a nunnery go.

757
00:30:08,808 --> 00:30:11,243
MIKE:
Well, actually,
I may go to grad school.

758
00:30:12,745 --> 00:30:15,147
- [SOBBING]

759
00:30:15,182 --> 00:30:19,318
Oh, what a noble mind
is here o'er thrown.

760
00:30:19,352 --> 00:30:21,453
The courtier's, soldier's,
scholar's eye,

761
00:30:21,487 --> 00:30:25,392
tongue, sword, expectancy
and rose of the fair state!

762
00:30:25,425 --> 00:30:30,128
Glass of fashion
and the mould of form all down.

763
00:30:30,162 --> 00:30:31,763
Oh, woe!

764
00:30:31,797 --> 00:30:33,232
MIKE:
Whoa!

765
00:30:33,265 --> 00:30:36,903
- Woe is me to have seen what
I have seen,

766
00:30:36,937 --> 00:30:40,207
see what I-- what I see.

767
00:30:40,240 --> 00:30:41,840
[SOBBING]

768
00:30:41,875 --> 00:30:42,842
SERVO:
Thank you for cooperating

769
00:30:42,875 --> 00:30:44,110
with the Copenhagen police.

770
00:30:44,143 --> 00:30:45,812
You can take off the wire now.

771
00:30:46,880 --> 00:30:47,847
- How now, Ophelia?

772
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:49,748
You did not tell us
what Lord Hamlet said.

773
00:30:49,748 --> 00:30:50,983
We heard it all.

774
00:30:52,485 --> 00:30:53,720
- He's far gone.

775
00:30:53,720 --> 00:30:54,953
Far gone.

776
00:30:54,987 --> 00:30:57,690
And truly in my youth
I suffered much extremity

777
00:30:57,723 --> 00:31:00,158
for love very near this.

778
00:31:00,192 --> 00:31:02,362
- Love?
CROW: Here? Now?

779
00:31:02,395 --> 00:31:05,765
- No, his affections
do not that way tend,

780
00:31:05,798 --> 00:31:07,000
nor what he speak,

781
00:31:07,033 --> 00:31:11,770
though it lacked form a little,
was not like madness.

782
00:31:11,803 --> 00:31:13,172
- I'll speak to him.

783
00:31:13,205 --> 00:31:15,542
MIKE:
I'm just gonna run
to the pop machine first.

784
00:31:15,575 --> 00:31:18,578
[♪♪♪]

785
00:31:21,915 --> 00:31:24,617
SERVO:
Rap artist Notorious K-I-N-G.

786
00:31:24,650 --> 00:31:26,785
[FOOTSTEPS]

787
00:31:26,818 --> 00:31:29,522
CROW:
Hi, I'm an Oliver Reed stand-in.

788
00:31:33,525 --> 00:31:34,593
- Woe is me...

789
00:31:34,627 --> 00:31:36,495
SERVO:
Woe is me!

790
00:31:36,528 --> 00:31:38,563
- ...to have seen
what I have seen...

791
00:31:38,598 --> 00:31:40,433
MIKE:
Mary Pickford as Ophelia.

792
00:31:40,467 --> 00:31:43,202
- ...see what I see.

793
00:31:46,138 --> 00:31:47,573
CROW:
Stupid, stupid Hamlet!

794
00:31:47,607 --> 00:31:50,108
What was I thinking?

795
00:31:50,142 --> 00:31:51,243
SERVO:
Hey, Kilroy!

796
00:31:51,277 --> 00:31:52,912
- To be or not to be?

797
00:31:52,945 --> 00:31:54,080
MIKE:
The verbal equivalent of

798
00:31:54,113 --> 00:31:55,782
♪ Dun dun dun daaa ♪

799
00:31:57,583 --> 00:31:59,318
- That is the question.

800
00:31:59,352 --> 00:32:01,087
CROW:
I'll take "To Be"
for fifty, Alex.

801
00:32:01,120 --> 00:32:04,457
- Whether 'tis
nobler in the mind

802
00:32:04,490 --> 00:32:08,060
to suffer the slings and arrows
of outrageous fortune...

803
00:32:08,093 --> 00:32:09,528
SERVO:
Starring Shelley Long
and Bette Middler.

804
00:32:09,562 --> 00:32:13,332
- ...or to take arms
against a sea of troubles,

805
00:32:13,365 --> 00:32:15,468
and by opposing, end them.

806
00:32:15,468 --> 00:32:18,037
MIKE:
Ow! My shin's right on
the edge of a stair.

807
00:32:18,070 --> 00:32:19,738
Oh!
- To die...

808
00:32:23,777 --> 00:32:25,010
to sleep.

809
00:32:25,043 --> 00:32:27,013
CROW:
Yeah, that's what we're doin'
right now, bub.

810
00:32:27,047 --> 00:32:28,147
- No more...

811
00:32:30,683 --> 00:32:33,920
and by a sleep to say
we end the heartache

812
00:32:33,953 --> 00:32:37,157
and the thousand natural shocks
that flesh is heir to...

813
00:32:37,190 --> 00:32:38,925
MIKE:
Okay, we need a predicate now.

814
00:32:38,958 --> 00:32:41,493
- ...'tis a consummation
devoutly to be wished.

815
00:32:41,527 --> 00:32:43,062
CROW:
Especially with Ophelia, man!

816
00:32:43,095 --> 00:32:44,797
[ALL CHUCKLING]

817
00:32:44,830 --> 00:32:46,065
- To die...

818
00:32:49,235 --> 00:32:50,268
to sleep...

819
00:32:50,302 --> 00:32:51,970
SERVO: To sleeeep!
MIKE: Whoa!

820
00:32:52,005 --> 00:32:53,773
CROW:
That's an old chestnut.

821
00:32:53,807 --> 00:32:54,773
- ...to sleep...

822
00:32:54,807 --> 00:32:56,208
SERVO: [WHISPERING]
To sleeeep!

823
00:32:56,242 --> 00:32:57,610
MIKE: [CHUCKLING]
Okay.

824
00:32:57,643 --> 00:32:59,812
- ...a chance to dream.

825
00:32:59,845 --> 00:33:01,480
CROW:
...the impossible dream!

826
00:33:01,513 --> 00:33:03,850
- Aye, there's the rub!

827
00:33:03,883 --> 00:33:05,117
MIKE:
I knew I had some rub left.

828
00:33:05,150 --> 00:33:07,487
- For in that sleep of death,
what dreams may come

829
00:33:07,520 --> 00:33:09,455
when we have
shuffled off this mortal coil

830
00:33:09,488 --> 00:33:10,790
must give us pause.

831
00:33:10,823 --> 00:33:13,558
There's the respect that
makes calamity of so long life,

832
00:33:13,592 --> 00:33:16,028
for who would bear
the whips and scorns of time,

833
00:33:16,062 --> 00:33:18,798
the oppressor's wrong,
the proud man's contumely,

834
00:33:18,832 --> 00:33:20,867
the pangs of despised love,

835
00:33:20,900 --> 00:33:23,068
the law's delay,
the insolence of office,

836
00:33:23,102 --> 00:33:26,372
and the spurns that patient
merit of the unworthy takes

837
00:33:26,405 --> 00:33:30,643
when he himself might his
quietus make with a bare bodkin?

838
00:33:30,677 --> 00:33:31,810
CROW: [CHUCKLING]
He said bare bodkin!

839
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:33,145
[ALL CHUCKLING]

840
00:33:33,178 --> 00:33:35,013
- Who would fardels bear...

841
00:33:35,080 --> 00:33:36,015
MIKE:
Fardels!

842
00:33:36,048 --> 00:33:37,750
- ...to grunt and sweat under
a weary life

843
00:33:37,817 --> 00:33:41,620
but that the dread
of something after death,

844
00:33:41,653 --> 00:33:44,157
the undiscovered country from
whose bourn

845
00:33:44,190 --> 00:33:48,460
no traveler returns
puzzles the will

846
00:33:48,493 --> 00:33:50,963
and makes us rather bear
those ills we have

847
00:33:50,997 --> 00:33:52,132
than fly to others...

848
00:33:52,165 --> 00:33:53,632
SERVO:
Sum up!

849
00:33:53,665 --> 00:33:56,168
- ...that we know not of?

850
00:33:58,003 --> 00:34:02,675
Thus conscience does make
cowards of us all,

851
00:34:02,708 --> 00:34:04,777
and thus the native hue
of resolution

852
00:34:04,810 --> 00:34:07,513
is sicklied o'er
with the pale cast of thought,

853
00:34:07,547 --> 00:34:09,915
and enterprises
of great pith and moment

854
00:34:09,948 --> 00:34:12,218
with this regard
their currents turn awry

855
00:34:12,252 --> 00:34:16,488
and lose the name of action.

856
00:34:16,522 --> 00:34:18,223
MIKE:
So, I'm a chicken
for not stabbing myself.

857
00:34:18,257 --> 00:34:20,092
That's all you needed to say!

858
00:34:21,193 --> 00:34:22,228
SERVO: D'oh!
CROW: Oh!

859
00:34:22,262 --> 00:34:23,395
MIKE:
Whoa!

860
00:34:23,428 --> 00:34:25,230
SERVO:
What's worse than clowns?

861
00:34:25,263 --> 00:34:26,965
Danish clowns.

862
00:34:26,998 --> 00:34:28,700
CROW:
Danish clowns, the damp, smelly,

863
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:31,470
silverfish-infested basement
of the clown world.

864
00:34:31,503 --> 00:34:32,938
[SERVO CHUCKLING]

865
00:34:32,972 --> 00:34:34,807
MIKE:
Okay, out. Out! Out!

866
00:34:34,840 --> 00:34:37,777
All of you, get out.
You, get out! Out!

867
00:34:37,810 --> 00:34:39,978
[♪♪♪]

868
00:34:41,513 --> 00:34:43,415
SERVO:
It's a herd of Hamlets!

869
00:34:46,352 --> 00:34:48,287
CROW:
We can't get rid of them.
It's hopeless.

870
00:34:52,492 --> 00:34:54,027
SERVO:
It's Hamlet Man!

871
00:34:54,060 --> 00:34:55,027
CROW:
Daa daa daa daaaa!

872
00:34:55,060 --> 00:34:56,562
- Welcome, masters.

873
00:34:56,628 --> 00:34:57,563
Welcome all.

874
00:34:57,597 --> 00:34:59,198
CROW:
Except you, condom-hat there.

875
00:34:59,265 --> 00:35:02,802
[FOOTSTEPS]

876
00:35:02,835 --> 00:35:05,337
- I am glad to see you well.

877
00:35:05,370 --> 00:35:06,572
Welcome good friends.

878
00:35:06,605 --> 00:35:07,940
SERVO:
Nice to see
the Hostess Sno Balls.

879
00:35:07,973 --> 00:35:10,108
- Old friend,
thy face is valanced

880
00:35:10,142 --> 00:35:11,610
since I saw thee last.

881
00:35:11,643 --> 00:35:12,612
- [CHUCKLING]

882
00:35:12,645 --> 00:35:14,080
- What, my young lady!

883
00:35:14,113 --> 00:35:15,080
Your ladyship...

884
00:35:15,113 --> 00:35:16,315
MIKE:
How's lesbianism going?

885
00:35:16,348 --> 00:35:19,185
- ...is nearer to heaven
by the altitude of a chopine

886
00:35:19,218 --> 00:35:20,620
than when I saw you last.

887
00:35:20,653 --> 00:35:23,923
Pray God, your voice
like a piece of uncurrent gold

888
00:35:23,957 --> 00:35:26,392
be not cracked within the ring.

889
00:35:26,425 --> 00:35:28,828
- I hope not so, my lord.

890
00:35:28,862 --> 00:35:30,228
- Welcome all.

891
00:35:30,262 --> 00:35:32,532
We'll e'en to it
like French falconers,

892
00:35:32,565 --> 00:35:33,765
fly at anything we see.

893
00:35:33,798 --> 00:35:35,300
We'll have a speech straight.

894
00:35:35,333 --> 00:35:37,937
Come, give us a taste
of your quality.

895
00:35:37,970 --> 00:35:40,072
CROW:
I said 'quality' not 'idiocy.'

896
00:35:40,105 --> 00:35:41,107
[♪♪♪]

897
00:35:41,140 --> 00:35:42,140
- Well?

898
00:35:43,342 --> 00:35:44,843
A passionate speech.

899
00:35:44,877 --> 00:35:46,245
SERVO:
Come here. We gotta talk.

900
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:50,348
- Can you play
The Murder of Gonzago?

901
00:35:50,382 --> 00:35:51,717
- Aye, my lord.

902
00:35:51,750 --> 00:35:53,252
- We'll have
that tomorrow night.

903
00:35:53,285 --> 00:35:54,320
You could, for a need...

904
00:35:54,353 --> 00:35:55,622
CROW:
Lose the clowns.

905
00:35:55,655 --> 00:35:57,890
- ...study a speech
of some dozen or 16 lines,

906
00:35:57,923 --> 00:36:00,225
which I would set down
and insert in it.

907
00:36:00,258 --> 00:36:01,760
Could you not?
CROW: Hey! Hey! Hey!

908
00:36:01,793 --> 00:36:05,230
- Aye, my lord.
- Very well.

909
00:36:06,232 --> 00:36:07,367
MIKE:
Yeah,
and I want Elizabeth Berkeley

910
00:36:07,400 --> 00:36:09,735
to play the lead, okay?

911
00:36:09,768 --> 00:36:12,772
[♪♪♪]

912
00:36:16,142 --> 00:36:17,243
- That's an excellent idea.

913
00:36:17,277 --> 00:36:19,078
- Well, thank you.
- Hey, where have you guys been?

914
00:36:19,112 --> 00:36:20,547
I haven't
seen you around at all.

915
00:36:20,613 --> 00:36:21,580
- Oh, sorry Mike.

916
00:36:21,613 --> 00:36:22,548
We've been in the middle
of rehearsals

917
00:36:22,582 --> 00:36:23,848
for our own version of Hamlet.

918
00:36:23,883 --> 00:36:26,318
It's gonna be sort of a modern
abstract interpretation

919
00:36:26,352 --> 00:36:27,320
sort of thing, you know.

920
00:36:27,353 --> 00:36:28,553
- Oh, so kind of
like the works

921
00:36:28,587 --> 00:36:31,123
of Richard Schechner
or Heiner Muller

922
00:36:31,157 --> 00:36:32,725
or, well,
countless college troupes.

923
00:36:32,758 --> 00:36:34,960
- Oh, yeah.
It's a timeless drama, Mike.

924
00:36:34,993 --> 00:36:36,795
Everyone should
take a shot at it.

925
00:36:36,828 --> 00:36:37,863
- Yeah, there's just so many
ways

926
00:36:37,897 --> 00:36:39,065
to render the play, Mike.

927
00:36:39,098 --> 00:36:40,532
- We even got as far as

928
00:36:40,567 --> 00:36:42,067
story boarding a few ideas.

929
00:36:42,100 --> 00:36:43,068
- Now, Mike, help us out there.

930
00:36:43,102 --> 00:36:44,503
Would you get those?
- Yeah, sure.

931
00:36:44,537 --> 00:36:45,503
- Now, here's what
we came up with

932
00:36:45,537 --> 00:36:47,940
for our scuba diving version.

933
00:36:47,973 --> 00:36:50,375
Pretty powerful stuff, huh?

934
00:36:50,408 --> 00:36:52,645
SERVO:
Then we considered
a bucket-head Hamlet.

935
00:36:52,678 --> 00:36:53,678
CROW:
The buckets, of course,

936
00:36:53,712 --> 00:36:55,748
symbolizing modern man's
faceless conformity.

937
00:36:55,782 --> 00:36:57,115
SERVO:
Yeah, but it didn't
really pan out.

938
00:36:57,148 --> 00:36:58,783
Well, then we were right
in the middle of rehearsals

939
00:36:58,817 --> 00:37:00,587
with our all-furniture version.

940
00:37:00,620 --> 00:37:02,955
- Oh, we were having
so much fun!

941
00:37:02,988 --> 00:37:05,792
The sofa that was playing
Gertrude was a delight!

942
00:37:05,825 --> 00:37:06,792
- Yes, but then our backers

943
00:37:06,825 --> 00:37:08,493
pulled out just days
before the opening.

944
00:37:08,527 --> 00:37:10,428
The footstools
were pretty upset.

945
00:37:10,462 --> 00:37:11,597
- Well, I think
all the furniture was.

946
00:37:11,630 --> 00:37:12,665
- Yeah, they were.

947
00:37:12,698 --> 00:37:13,832
But-- but that brings us

948
00:37:13,865 --> 00:37:15,668
to our percussion version
of Hamlet.

949
00:37:15,702 --> 00:37:17,803
The bongos here
represent Ophelia.

950
00:37:17,837 --> 00:37:20,305
- And obviously,
these maracas are Hamlet.

951
00:37:20,338 --> 00:37:23,108
Now, allow us to perform
a part of Act III, Scene 1.

952
00:37:23,142 --> 00:37:24,210
Thank you.
- Thank you.

953
00:37:24,243 --> 00:37:25,978
[DRUMMING]

954
00:37:26,012 --> 00:37:27,380
[RATTLING]

955
00:37:27,413 --> 00:37:29,348
[SERVO GRUNTING]

956
00:37:31,517 --> 00:37:32,618
[BUZZING]

957
00:37:32,652 --> 00:37:33,987
- Oh, excuse me...
we got movie sign.

958
00:37:34,020 --> 00:37:35,988
We can pick this up later.

959
00:37:36,022 --> 00:37:37,122
- We're just getting
to the murder, Mike.

960
00:37:37,155 --> 00:37:38,157
Hang on.

961
00:37:51,637 --> 00:37:52,705
CROW:
Now is the winter of our...

962
00:37:52,738 --> 00:37:55,340
Damn, wrong play.

963
00:37:55,373 --> 00:37:57,142
- About, my brains!

964
00:37:57,175 --> 00:37:58,910
CROW:
Upon which I sit. [CHUCKLING]

965
00:37:58,943 --> 00:37:59,978
- I'll have these players

966
00:38:00,012 --> 00:38:01,413
play something like
the murder of my father

967
00:38:01,447 --> 00:38:03,582
before mine uncle.

968
00:38:03,615 --> 00:38:06,585
I'll observe his looks,
I'll tent him to the quick.

969
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:08,753
If he but blench,
I'll know my course.

970
00:38:08,787 --> 00:38:10,923
MIKE:
If he but parboil, well...

971
00:38:10,957 --> 00:38:13,325
- The spirit that I've seen
may be a devil

972
00:38:13,358 --> 00:38:15,828
and perhaps out of my weakness
and my melancholy

973
00:38:15,862 --> 00:38:17,195
abuses me to damn me.

974
00:38:17,228 --> 00:38:19,298
I'll have grounds
more relative than this.

975
00:38:19,332 --> 00:38:20,933
SERVO:
He should start journaling.

976
00:38:21,933 --> 00:38:25,170
- The play is the thing...

977
00:38:25,203 --> 00:38:27,105
CROW:
A badda badda badda bing.

978
00:38:27,138 --> 00:38:33,278
- ...wherein I'll catch
the conscience of the king.

979
00:38:33,312 --> 00:38:35,682
SERVO:
A ring-a-ding ding ding ding.

980
00:38:36,682 --> 00:38:38,783
MIKE:
Let's see.
Boy, girl, boy, girl, me.

981
00:38:38,817 --> 00:38:39,818
Okay.

982
00:38:43,322 --> 00:38:44,690
CROW:
Whoa! The dinner rush is here.

983
00:38:44,723 --> 00:38:46,492
Look lively, people.

984
00:38:49,562 --> 00:38:50,797
MIKE:
It's the slow-walking race.

985
00:38:50,830 --> 00:38:53,865
In the front,
Lillian and Bob are losing.

986
00:38:53,898 --> 00:38:55,000
SERVO:
Listen.

987
00:38:55,033 --> 00:38:56,735
The Hamlets always have
a kick-ass party table.

988
00:38:56,768 --> 00:38:58,370
MIKE:
Yeah!

989
00:38:58,403 --> 00:39:01,140
[CROW HUMMING]

990
00:39:01,173 --> 00:39:03,442
CROW:
Um, they can see you, Hamlet.

991
00:39:05,577 --> 00:39:07,513
MIKE:
Oh, shoot.
Frank Rich is out there.

992
00:39:07,580 --> 00:39:08,913
- Come! 'Tis ready.

993
00:39:08,947 --> 00:39:10,482
SERVO:
We have a small
but spirited house.

994
00:39:10,515 --> 00:39:11,617
